# Phase 46 — Jest's own database, entirely separate from the shared dev database .env points at.
# Never contains real secrets (nothing here protects anything real), so — unlike .env — this file
# IS committed: every developer and CI gets deterministic, isolated test infrastructure with zero
# manual setup. See jest.setup.env.ts for how this gets merged with .env (JWT secrets etc. still
# come from there; only these two keys are overridden).
#
# Root cause this fixes: test-utils/fixtures.ts's createTestPlan() (and several other fixtures)
# create real documents with no cleanup in many test files. Every one of those was landing in the
# SAME MongoDB database the dev server and this repo's own /public/plans endpoint read from,
# because Jest had no database of its own — that's the actual source of the previously-observed
# "polluted local plans catalog" (stray isActive:true Plan documents with empty pricing). Pointing
# Jest at its own database makes that contamination structurally impossible going forward, without
# changing a single test file's fixture/cleanup logic.
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/restaurant_platform_test
# A different logical Redis database (same server, no second Redis process needed) — isolates
# BullMQ queue state, rate-limiter buckets, and refresh-token storage from whatever the dev server
# is doing in DB 0 at the same time.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1
